      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Simulated: the AI's side",
      "items": [
        "codex is a stand-in (sim/bin/codex): it reads the files Codex loads, starts the MCP server, makes one model call, calls budget_status, spawn_agent and deliver, writes the four files",
        "Its own steps take milliseconds: a real session lasts as long as the AI works, and that time is not shown here",
        "Everything else ran for real: Frontier's code, the OpenAI API (3 calls), the Scaleway and Runpod offer APIs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "How the bars are timed",
      "items": [
        "Seconds since the trace's first event; the hook (sim/hook/sitecustomize.py) records calls, not returns",
        "A function ends at the next call on its thread at the same or a shallower depth, else at the thread's last event",
        "A subprocess ends at the next event of the thread that waits for it; a harness span runs from one step to the next",
        "Not traced: the serve_forever threads of the gateway and the filter, the filter's byte relay, process exits"
      ]
    }
